# Brand text buttons

Reave pill CTAs share **one visual system**. Change `src/styles/brand.css` once → every filled / solid / glass / danger button updates.

## Three layers — use the right one

| Surface | Use | Do not |
|---------|-----|--------|
| **Astro / SSR markup** | `<BrandBtn variant="glass" href="…">Label</BrandBtn>` | Hand-roll `<button class="brand-btn …">` unless BrandBtn cannot fit (rare) |
| **Admin client JS** | `createBrandBtn({ variant: 'filled', label: '…', onClick })` | Hand-roll gradient pills, `font: inherit` CTAs, or duplicate `.dash-panel-btn` visuals |
| **Legacy HTML strings** | `class="brand-btn"` / `brand-btn brand-btn-glass` via `brandBtnClasses()` | `cs-wizard-btn`, one-off pill CSS |

Variant class map (keep in sync):
- `src/lib/brandButton.ts`
- `public/admin/brand-button.js`

## Variants

- `filled` — gradient pill (default primary)
- `solid` — flat ink/bone fill
- `glass` — frosted secondary
- `danger` — destructive confirm

Layout-only hooks (margin, flex) may add extra classes (`dash-panel-btn`, `admin-setup-alert-btn`) — **never** re-declare font, gradient, or radius there.

## Legacy aliases still work

`.de-btn-primary`, `.prof-btn-secondary`, `.os-dialog-btn--primary`, etc. alias the same rules in `brand.css`. Prefer `createBrandBtn` / `BrandBtn` for new code; when touching legacy markup, switch to the component path if easy.

## Out of scope

Site-themed landings (`vet-btn*`, `pack-btn*`, marketing `*-btn` wrappers) intentionally use local accent colors. Do not force BrandBtn there unless unifying that site to core brand tokens.

## Icon-only chrome

Toolbar circles use `IOS_ICONS` + `createIosIconBtn` / `createFabNewBtn` — not BrandBtn.
